# Copy this file to key.properties and set your own signing configuration.
# key.properties is gitignored so that secrets are never committed.
# If the file is absent, the release build falls back to debug signing
# (suitable for local development only).
#
# WARNING: do NOT leave the placeholder values below (your_store_password /
# your_key_password) in your key.properties. Gradle will accept the file as
# "configured" and silently fall back to debug signing when the password
# does not unlock the keystore, producing a "release" APK signed with the
# Android default debug key. `make build-release` and the release CI now
# call scripts/verify-release-keystore.sh to detect this, but the safest
# habit is to fill in real credentials immediately after copying.
#
# See docs/build-guide.md for keystore generation instructions.
storePassword=your_store_password
keyPassword=your_key_password
keyAlias=release
storeFile=../keystore/release.jks
